   "hint": "Collect arguments until you have <code>fn.length</code> of them.",
   "answer": "Return a function that gathers arguments. When it has at least <code>fn.length</code> arguments, call <code>fn</code> with them. Otherwise return another function that adds more arguments to the ones so far.",
   "explain": "<p><code>fn.length</code> is the number of declared parameters, not counting rest or default parameters. Currying is used to build small configured helpers, such as <code>const getJson = request(\"GET\")</code>.</p>",
   "kind": "Coding",
   "acode": "function curry(fn) {\n  return function curried(...args) {\n    return args.length >= fn.length\n      ? fn.apply(this, args)\n      : (...more) => curried.apply(this, [...args, ...more]);\n  };\n}"
