   "explain": "<p>A <code>try</code> block only catches errors from promises that are awaited inside it. <code>try { doAsync() } catch {}</code> without <code>await</code> catches nothing.</p><p>In test runners an unhandled rejection usually fails the run, sometimes in a different test from the one that caused it, which makes it hard to trace.</p>"
