   "hint": "A loop with try and catch, and a wait that doubles each time.",
   "answer": "Loop up to <code>attempts</code> times. Return the result when <code>fn</code> succeeds. On failure, rethrow if it was the last attempt, otherwise wait <code>delay * 2 ** i</code> milliseconds and try again.",
   "explain": "<p>Only retry errors that can be temporary, such as a 503 or a network reset, and never a 400. Add random jitter to the delay so that many clients do not retry at the same moment.</p><p>In tests, retrying hides real problems. Prefer waiting for a condition, such as Playwright <code>expect.poll</code>, over retrying whole actions.</p>",
   "kind": "Coding",
