   "answer": "For fetch, pass <code>signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000)</code>, which aborts the request after 5 seconds with a <code>TimeoutError</code>. For any promise, use <code>Promise.race</code> with a promise that rejects after <code>ms</code>, and clear the timer when the race ends.",
   "explain": "<p>The difference matters: aborting a fetch really stops the request, while racing only stops waiting for it, and the work carries on in the background.</p>",
