   "answer": "Return a new promise. For each item, wrap it with <code>Promise.resolve</code>, store its value at its own index, and count finished items. Resolve when the count reaches the length, reject on the first failure, and resolve at once for an empty list.",
   "explain": "<p>Using the index rather than <code>push</code> is the key detail, because promises finish in any order. <code>Promise.resolve</code> lets the list contain plain values as well as promises.</p>",
